## Websocket Events

The system uses Socket.io for real-time communication between the server and client:

### Server to Client Events

| Event | Description | Payload Example |
|-------|-------------|----------------|
| `step-result` | Result of a step execution | `{success: true, stepIndex: 2, output: "Clicked button successfully"}` |
| `human-handoff` | Request for human intervention | `{active: true, message: "Please complete the CAPTCHA", screenshot: "data:image/png;base64,..."}` |
| `execution-progress` | Overall execution progress | `{completed: 3, total: 5, currentStep: "Filling login form"}` |
| `browser-error` | Error in browser execution | `{message: "Timeout waiting for selector", selector: "#login-button"}` |
| `script-generation` | Script generation progress | `{status: "completed", script: "// Generated script..."}` |

### Client to Server Events

| Event | Description | Payload Example |
|-------|-------------|----------------|
| `run-step` | Request to run a specific step | `{scriptId: "script_123", stepIndex: 2}` |
| `run-script` | Request to run entire script | `{scriptId: "script_123", options: {headless: false}}` |
| `continue-after-handoff` | Signal to continue after human action | `{}` |
| `cancel-execution` | Request to cancel execution | `{scriptId: "script_123"}` |
| `generate-script` | Request to generate a script | `{task: "Go to example.com and extract all links"}` |

Example server-side Socket.io implementation:
```javascript
// Set up Socket.io connection
io.on('connection', (socket) => {
  console.log('Client connected');
  
  // Store the socket connection for later use
  const socketId = socket.id;
  activeConnections[socketId] = socket;
  
  // Handle client disconnection
  socket.on('disconnect', () => {
    console.log('Client disconnected');
    delete activeConnections[socketId];
  });
  
  // Event: Run a step in the browser
  socket.on('run-step', async (data) => {
    try {
      // Validate input
      if (!data || !data.scriptId || data.stepIndex === undefined) {
        socket.emit('error', { message: 'Invalid step execution request' });
        return;
      }
      
      console.log(`Running step ${data.stepIndex} for script ${data.scriptId}`);
      
      // Get the script from repository
      const scriptRepo = getScriptRepository();
      const script = await scriptRepo.getScript(data.scriptId);
      
      if (!script || !script.steps || !script.steps[data.stepIndex]) {
        socket.emit('error', { message: 'Script or step not found' });
        return;
      }
      
      // Execute the step
      const step = script.steps[data.stepIndex];
      const result = await executeStepInBrowser(step);
      
      // Send the result back to the client
      socket.emit('step-result', {
        success: true,
        stepIndex: data.stepIndex,
        output: result.output,
        screenshot: result.screenshot
      });
      
      // Update script execution metadata
      script.metadata.lastRun = new Date().toISOString();
      script.metadata.runCount = (script.metadata.runCount || 0) + 1;
      await scriptRepo.saveScript(script, data.scriptId);
      
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error executing step:', error);
      socket.emit('step-result', {
        success: false,
        stepIndex: data.stepIndex,
        error: error.message
      });
    }
  });
  
  // Event: Continue after human handoff
  socket.on('continue-after-handoff', () => {
    console.log('Continuing after human handoff');
    if (humanHandoffResolve) {
      humanHandoffResolve(true);
      humanHandoffResolve = null;
      inHumanHandoffMode = false;
    }
  });
  
  // Event: Cancel execution
  socket.on('cancel-execution', (data) => {
    console.log(`Cancelling execution for script ${data.scriptId}`);
    
    // Implement cancellation logic here
    // ...
    
    socket.emit('execution-cancelled', {
      scriptId: data.scriptId,
      message: 'Execution cancelled successfully'
    });
  });
});
```

